{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"Detection, from the fields this investigation already read rather than from a new API: GetConfiguration and Stats report the node's in-memory configuration and its index (api.go 1231-1237 and the GetConfiguration accessor), so the state is found by comparing that configuration with the configuration a peer reports or with the newest configuration entry in the node's own store, not by a threshold on indexes. The two forms observed here are an empty in-memory configuration (the empty case, seen as zero servers and zero peers while the node still holds a complete log) and an in-memory configuration older than the newest configuration entry in that node's log (the stale case, e.g. two servers while peers report three or four). One caution against a false positive: latest_configuration_index being below commit_index is normal, because a configuration entry stays the latest until a later configuration entry appears while ordinary entries continue to commit, so that comparison alone does not indicate this state.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
